The arbitrary-word classification in Theorem 6.2 agreed on all words
through original-root length $D+2$, for $92366$ source/word comparisons.
Every permutation, label assignment and $q=0,\ldots,r$ was checked for
the recollection construction when $D\le2$, giving $2048$ decoder
checks. The $D=3$ history total in the table is computed from the checked
fiber sizes times $(2b_c)!$; its permutations were not all enumerated.
Direct finite substitution of each actual $v$ and $\pi_D(v)$ agreed on
all $W_D$ readouts for $k=0,\ldots,2D$ and $D=1,2,3$, totaling
$71442$ comparisons. These finite checks can reject faulty local
constructions; they do not prove arbitrary-word, all-depth, optimality or
all-count assertions. The ordinary proofs and credited suppliers carry
those quantifiers.

